### Brand API walkthrough
### Run `make dev` first. Execute these requests in order in VS Code REST Client.
### Each request disables REST Client's cookie jar; explicit Cookie headers keep A and B sessions separate.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5173/api/v1
@password = password1

### No session: 401 unauthorized
# @no-cookie-jar
GET {{baseUrl}}/brands

### Create user A and capture koi_session
# @no-cookie-jar
# @name signupA
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"brand-a-{{$guid}}@example.com","password":"{{password}}"}

### Confirm A's session identity before brand requests: 200 A
# @no-cookie-jar
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Cookie: {{signupA.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

### A has no brands yet: 200 with empty items and zero totalItems
# @no-cookie-jar
GET {{baseUrl}}/brands
Cookie: {{signupA.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

### Country codes accepted by the current validator: 200 array containing IT
# @no-cookie-jar
GET {{baseUrl}}/brands/countries
Cookie: {{signupA.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

### Create A's brand: 201; spoofed user_id is ignored
# @no-cookie-jar
# @name createA
POST {{baseUrl}}/brands
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{signupA.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

{"user_id":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000","name":"Koi","domain":"koi.dev","github_repo":"https://github.com/koihq/koi","country":"IT","description":"Koi measures brand visibility in AI answers."}

### A sees only A's brand: 200 with one item and totalItems 1
# @no-cookie-jar
GET {{baseUrl}}/brands
Cookie: {{signupA.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

### A's out-of-range page: 200 with empty items and currentPage 2
# @no-cookie-jar
GET {{baseUrl}}/brands?page=2&pageSize=1
Cookie: {{signupA.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

### Read A's brand: 200
# @no-cookie-jar
GET {{baseUrl}}/brands/{{createA.response.body.$.id}}
Cookie: {{signupA.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

### Change an editable field: 200; user_id remains A's
# @no-cookie-jar
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/brands/{{createA.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{signupA.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

{"description":"Koi measures mentions and citations in AI answers.","user_id":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"}

### Invalid country: 400 validation with country field error
# @no-cookie-jar
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/brands/{{createA.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{signupA.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

{"country":"ZZ"}

### Second brand: 409 brand_limit_reached
# @no-cookie-jar
POST {{baseUrl}}/brands
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{signupA.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

{"name":"Second","domain":"second.dev","country":"IT"}

### Create user B and capture a separate session
# @no-cookie-jar
# @name signupB
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"brand-b-{{$guid}}@example.com","password":"{{password}}"}

### Confirm B's session identity before cross-user requests: 200 B
# @no-cookie-jar
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Cookie: {{signupB.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

### B has no brands: 200 with empty items and zero totalItems
# @no-cookie-jar
GET {{baseUrl}}/brands
Cookie: {{signupB.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

### B cannot read A's brand: 404 not_found
# @no-cookie-jar
GET {{baseUrl}}/brands/{{createA.response.body.$.id}}
Cookie: {{signupB.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

### B cannot edit A's brand: 404 not_found
# @no-cookie-jar
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/brands/{{createA.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{signupB.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

{"name":"Stolen"}

### Create B's brand: 201
# @no-cookie-jar
# @name createB
POST {{baseUrl}}/brands
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{signupB.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

{"name":"B Project","github_repo":"https://github.com/koihq/b-project","country":"IT"}

### A cannot read B's brand: 404 not_found
# @no-cookie-jar
GET {{baseUrl}}/brands/{{createB.response.body.$.id}}
Cookie: {{signupA.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

### A cannot edit B's brand: 404 not_found
# @no-cookie-jar
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/brands/{{createB.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{signupA.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

{"name":"Stolen"}
